    "dex.cinderle": "It kindles itself each dawn from yesterday's ash, a small reliable downbeat of warmth. Hearth-keepers along Route 4 leave their grates open on cold nights.",
    "dex.frostrel": "It hums fractions of a degree below the air around it, and frost writes the staff lines. Children race to read tomorrow's window-music.",
    "dex.glacialto": "A glacier in alto register, it sings one phrase per winter and finishes none of them. The unfinished cadence is the coast's oldest open question.",
    "dex.madrigale": "It sings five-part harmony alone, each petal-mouth carrying a line. Arbor Vale's choir lost its festival title to one and framed the scoresheet.",
    "dex.pyrelodie": "Its updraft carries its own melody line a beat ahead of it, announcing arrivals it hasn't made yet. Brushfires follow it politely, single file.",
    "dex.requiemoth": "It appears where songs end early — closed halls, dead air, the Quiet Coast. Its wings hold the last four bars of whatever wasn't finished.",
    "dex.staccatto": "Every footfall lands detached and exact, sixteenth after sixteenth. Calando's clock-makers keep one in the shop window instead of a metronome.",
    "dex.terracant": "Terraced gardens grow up its back, tended by families who have never seen it move. Twice a century it stands, apologizes, and lies down somewhere else.",
    "dex.tidempo": "Storm tides charge it; calm ones spend it. The harbor master reads its glow like a pressure gauge with opinions.",
    "dex.vesperbat": "It hunts in the evening rests, striking only where the night's music pauses. Vesper-bell ringers consider it a colleague.",
