    "arbor.elder.after": "A Treble clef from Mirelle. She doesn't hand those to weeds.",
    "arbor.elder.hint": "Mirelle prunes her challengers like saplings. Show her your roots first.",
    "calando.harbor.after": "Three clefs! The tide tables say good things about you.",
    "calando.harbor.hint": "Bram conducts two boats at once and his hall the same way. Bring a pair.",
    "echo1.ask": "Pausa's anchor echo is mine to keep. Earn the hearing.",
    "echo1.done": "The echo holds. So far.",
    "echo1.grant": "The first echo is yours. Seven keepers left. We talk, between us. We'll know you're coming.",
    "echo1.locked": "The anchor ledger stays shut until you carry a clef.",
    "echo1.story": "Listen: the pillar under Pausa hums a fourth flat. It didn't, forty years ago. Remember that when someone tells you the song keeps itself.",
    "echo2.ask": "Arbor Vale grew around its anchor like bark around a nail. Hear it?",
    "echo2.done": "The nail holds. The bark grows.",
    "echo2.grant": "The vale's echo, kept and given. Mind the drift.",
    "echo2.locked": "Two clefs before the vale's echo. Rules older than me.",
    "echo2.story": "Every spring the bloom opens a day later than the year before. The vale calls it weather. The keepers call it drift.",
    "echo3.ask": "You've heard the dead air out there. Now hear what it ate.",
    "echo3.done": "Half a song, still safe.",
    "echo3.grant": "The coast's echo. Half a song, heavier than most whole ones.",
    "echo3.locked": "Three clefs. The coast's echo isn't for tourists.",
    "echo3.story": "There was a lighthouse song here once — four bars, every night, three hundred years. The Caesura took it mid-phrase. The keepers keep the missing half.",
    "hall2.arranger.after": "The Maestro's tempo is slower than it looks. Mind it.",
    "hall2.arranger.defeat": "Rearranged…",
    "hall2.arranger.intro": "I arrange the hall's bouquets — and its upsets.",
    "hall2.mirelle.after": "Mirelle: Water finds the coast road south. So do trainers worth the trip.",
    "hall2.mirelle.badge": "Mirelle: The Treble clef. Second of eight — the canopy gets thinner from here.",
    "hall2.mirelle.clearing": "Mirelle: And the Clearing Chord. Brush parts for those who ask in key.",
    "hall2.mirelle.defeat": "Mirelle: Well rooted. Well grown.",
    "hall2.mirelle.intro": "Mirelle: Patience is just tempo you commit to. Shall we see yours?",
    "hall2.pruner.after": "Grow on through.",
    "hall2.pruner.defeat": "Clipped!",
    "hall2.pruner.intro": "Every stem in this maze answers to the shears. You won't.",
    "hall3.bram.after": "Bram: The road north thins out. The company you keep won't.",
    "hall3.bram.badge": "Bram: The Soprano clef, third of eight, and loudly earned.",
    "hall3.bram.defeat": "Bram: HA! Facts! Marvelous, ringing facts!",
    "hall3.bram.intro": "Bram: One voice is a claim. Two voices are a fact. Show me facts!",
    "hall3.bram.tunneling": "Bram: Take the Tunneling Bass too. Some doors are just rocks with opinions.",
    "hall3.duo_a.after": "Go on — Bram likes ensembles brave.",
    "hall3.duo_a.defeat": "Out of step, both of us!",
    "hall3.duo_a.intro": "We audition pairs only. Your two against my two!",
    "hall3.duo_b.after": "The Maestro's stage is yours.",
    "hall3.duo_b.defeat": "Beautifully voiced…",
    "hall3.duo_b.intro": "Counterpoint check: can your left hand trust your right?",
    "keyshift.1": "LOOK at her. A keyshifted Sirenetta! One in four thousand and ninety-six!",
    "keyshift.2": "Same notes as any other — but the whole phrase sits a key to the left. Collectors weep. I wept.",
    "keyshift.3": "If a wild Mote ever sounds… sideways to you? Ring everything you own at it.",
    "keyshift.again": "She's still keyshifted. I still weep.",
    "lull.1": "Lull: Don't mind me. I watch the new clefs. You can keep walking — most do.",
    "lull.2": "Lull: Or indulge me one match. I don't play to win. I play to ask.",
    "lull.3": "Lull: There it is. You attune beautifully. Question, though —",
    "lull.4": "Lull: What's the longest you've let one stay out of the bell?",
